{
  "about": "Whole numbers and decimals that do not fit, on every stack (the user, 2026-11-21: \"Value error, handler stops\"). A whole number is 64 bits; a decimal holds up to 28 places with a whole number of units that fits in 96 bits, as Rust and C# keep it. A result with more places than fit is rounded to the places that do (a tie to the even digit); a result that does not fit even with no places is a value error: the handler stops and the window says it. Each case gives the `kind` (whole or decimal), the `op` (+, -, *, div, mod or neg, which takes only `a`), `a`, `b` and the `result` as text, or `error` true.",
